# tests/semantic_snapshot_lineage_test.tg — third-audit item 11 +
# fourth-audit P0-1/P0-2/P0-3 (the persistent declaration lineage)
# end-to-end lane.
#
# The lineage model lives in tg_compiler/stable_ids.tg (StablePackageId /
# StableModuleId / DeclLineageId / DeclLineageStore / DeclContinuation /
# DeclMove, the move-stable StableDeclId identity over (package, lineage,
# kind), the exact-structural-key + explicit-continuation identity
# authority of fourth-audit P0-3 and the v2 atomic store), and the snapshot
# builder's store seam lives in tg_compiler/semantic_snapshot.tg
# (snapshot_stamp_decls — the def walk's declaration-stamping stage). This
# test drives snapshot_lineage_lane_check: ONE DeclLineageStore threaded
# across builds of the builder's stamping stage, pinning the P0-3
# behaviors —
#   * an EXACT structural key (unchanged package/module/kind/name) keeps its
#     id through nearby insertions and signature edits;
#   * an explicit DeclContinuation (or the edit-engine DeclMove applied
#     through stable_lineage_store_apply_move) always preserves identity —
#     a move between modules included — even when the signature changed;
#   * a delete of old(Int) followed by an unrelated same-signature creation
#     yields DIFFERENT ids in ALL cases (same revision, later revision,
#     after restart, or from a v1 legacy body): the automatic
#     same-signature/prev-revision rebinding is GONE (P0-3);
#   * the v2 save/load restart round-trip preserves the signature digest
#     words and the explicit continuations;
#   * (audit order item 5) the STABLE TEST identity (stable_test_id_of_decl)
#     is keyed by the test declaration's persistent lineage + test-kind: an
#     unrelated insertion keeps the digest while the declared name/attrs
#     ride as cargo, and a rename without a continuation is fresh;
# plus the no-speculation fallbacks. The helper returns mismatch rows
# (empty = the whole lane verifies), the sibling lane-check convention.
#
# Run with the repo root as the working directory:
#   tg test tests/semantic_snapshot_lineage_test.tg

use std::test::assert

use tg_compiler::semantic_snapshot::{snapshot_lineage_lane_check}

@test
def test_snapshot_lineage_continuity_lane() -> Unit
  let rows = snapshot_lineage_lane_check()
  assert(rows.len() == 0, "snapshot lineage lane mismatches: " + rows.join("; "))
end
